{{!
    @template tool_vae/compare_page

    The page "Comparer deux versions", below its heading: the section, the way to its history, the sentence that says which
    two versions and how much moved, a notification when a version is compared to itself, and the block of the comparison,
    which keeps white space as written (drawn whole by its own template).

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\compare_page. The template holds no logic. Every
    text and address is escaped (double braces), except two keys of HTML (triple braces): samehtml, a notification made by
    the core ($output->notification()); diffhtml, the block of the comparison drawn by the template tool_vae/compare_diff
    ($output->render()), which escapes every text of the two versions and marks what was added and removed.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * section - string, the section compared
    * history - {url, label}: the way to the history of the section
    * summary - string, which two versions, and how much moved
    * samehtml - false, or HTML: the notification that a version is compared to itself
    * diffhtml - string, HTML: the block of the comparison

    Example context (json):
    {
        "section": "Section: Objectives of the approach",
        "history": {"url": "https://example.com/admin/tool/vae/history.php?draftid=5", "label": "History and comparison"},
        "summary": "Version 1 compared to version 3: 2 words added, 1 removed.",
        "samehtml": false,
        "diffhtml": "<div class=\"tool-vae-diff border rounded p-3\">Je <del class=\"tool-vae-del\">prépare</del></div>"
    }
}}
<p>{{section}}</p>
{{#history}}
<p><a href="{{url}}">{{label}}</a></p>
{{/history}}
<p>{{summary}}</p>
{{#samehtml}}
{{{samehtml}}}
{{/samehtml}}
{{{diffhtml}}}
